      "sentences": [
        {
          "sid": "pronouns-t1-s01",
          "c": "我係阿明。",
          "j": "ngo5 hai6 aa3 ming4.",
          "e": "I am Ah Ming.",
          "note": "係 (hai6) means \"is / am / are\" — one word for all three. 我係 (ngo5 hai6) \"I am\", 你係 (nei5 hai6) \"you are\", 佢係 (keoi5 hai6) \"he is\". And 我 (ngo5) is both \"I\" and \"me\" — it never changes shape.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "I"
            },
            {
              "c": "係",
              "j": "hai6",
              "e": "am"
            },
            {
              "c": "阿明",
              "j": "aa3 ming4",
              "e": "Ah Ming (a name)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "pronouns-t1-s02",
          "c": "你係我嘅朋友。",
          "j": "nei5 hai6 ngo5 ge3 pang4 jau5.",
          "e": "You are my friend.",
          "note": "Add <b>嘅</b> (ge3) after a person-word to mean \"belonging to them\", like \"'s\" in English — 我嘅 (ngo5 ge3) \"my\", 你嘅 (nei5 ge3) \"your\", 佢嘅 (keoi5 ge3) \"his / her\".",
